                    AWS Global Footpint

Regions- Seperate Geographic areas which host AWS Daracenters. Provide greatest Fault Tolerance/sustainability & allow you to deploy workloads worldwide.

Availability Zones- Isolated locations in specific regions W/ their own Redundant Power/Networking/Low-Latancy Connectivity. They are physically seperated to reduce impacts of disasters. made up of MULTIPLE datacenters.
AWS likes to have 3 or more AZs per region typically.

Edge Locations- AWS data centers meant to help deliver extremely low latancy. Typically closer to End Users as opposed to Regions/AZs. They typically leverage "Points of Presence" & regional edge caches.

GovCloud Regions- Strictly for government cloud environments/services.

AZ IDs- MOST critical thing to know when planning to build multi-account infrustructure designs. (BEST PRACTICE)


                    Shared Responsibility Model & Well Architectured Framework

Security & compliance is a shared responsibility between AWS and Customers.



Customer is responsible for security IN the cloud. This includes:

Customer Data, platform, applications, idenity and access management. OS and Network/Firewall configurations. Client side data encryption & data integrity, Server side encryption (such as file system and data), and Networking traffic protection


AWS is responsible for security OF the cloud. This includes:

Software, compute, storage, databases, networking. Hardware/Global AWS infrustructure maintenance. Regions/AZs/Edge locations.

Well Architectured Framework is a set of principles that we shoula aim to apply to ALL AS-based workloads.

    Operational Excellence- Does the architecture work & will it continue to work? Support development, run workloads efficientyl, insight into operations, team continues to improve the suppotying processes & procedures to deliver business value

    Security- Taking advantage of technologies offeres to protect data, protect systems, and prtect assets. Maintaining ltraceability, applying security in layters, encrypting data in transit & at rest, keeping people away from your data.

    Cost optimization- Run your systems that deliver value, but operate at lowers price point for value. Adopt consumption model, measure overall efficiency, letting AWS handle heavy lifting for infrustructure.

    Reliability- Does the system work consistently and recover quickly. Ability for you/workload to perform correctly and consistently, be easily tested. Automate the recoveries from failure, testing your recovery procedures, scaling horizontally. PLAN FOR FAILURE, not perfection, if things fail there should be things in place to mitigate the failures rather than hoping it all works perfectly or all heck breaks loose.

    Performace Efficiency- working to remove bottlenecks and reduce your waste. Using correct computing resources, maintainging efficiency with scaling demands (like an e-commerce store with holidays coming), Using serverless architectures, deploying globally using AWS Regions, and experimenting often, are you make sure you're testing load balancing and testing new releases.

    Sustainability- Minimize environmental impacts from workloads. Reduce energy consumption, increasing efficiency across all components of a workload, maximizing the benefits from the provisioned resources, and minimizing the total resources required. Understand your impact, maximize your utilization and use managed services.


                    AWS Well-Architected Tool

What is it? A service providing a consistent process for measuring your architecture. Allows you to see how closely allignes with AWS Best Practices you are, assists with documenting the decisions and the "why" behind those, gives you recommendations for improving workloads, and helps design reliable, secure, efficient, and cost-effective solutions.


